 Parse the value as a boolean type instead of string type if it's a boolean.
 
+##### ignoreEmpty
+
+Type: `boolean`\
+Default: `false`
+
+```js
+import queryString from 'query-string';
+
+queryString.parse('?q=&page=2&flag', {ignoreEmpty: true});
+//=> {page: '2', flag: null}
+```
+
+Drop the parameters that have an empty value. A key without `=` has a `null` value, so it is kept.
+
+##### stripTracking
+
+Type: `boolean`\
+Default: `false`
+
+```js
+import queryString from 'query-string';
+
+queryString.parse('?q=shoes&utm_source=news&fbclid=abc&gclid=def', {stripTracking: true});
+//=> {q: 'shoes'}
+```
+
+Drop the tracking parameters: `utm_*`, `fbclid`, and `gclid`. The names are matched case-insensitively.
+
